This Directive applies to those categories of electrical equipment whose insulation and/or intended use or application is intended to meet the requirements of:
Type A2, B2, C2 or E2 of IEC 60364 Part 4;
Part 4-3 of BS EN 62447;
IEC TR 60617 for systems providing low temperature environments within the range provided in Annex ZA to this Directive;
IEC Tr 62257 for those systems providing both medium and high temperatures within the range covered by IEC/TR 62257 (for examples and definitions, see annex ZA).
the Directive relating to the health problems caused by electromagnetic disturbance with hazardous effects on the health;
the Council directive 89/686/EEC on equipment intended for working at low temperatures [1].
The standard conditions which apply for tests on the functionality and performance of electrical equipment are given in IEC 61260. These shall apply together with this Directive.
